<section class="alt" id="faqs"><div class="wrap narrow"><div class="sec-head rv center"><span class="eyebrow">FAQs</span><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can you manage my property if I live abroad?</summary><p>Yes. Services can be arranged for owners who live abroad or outside the property's location, subject to an agreed management scope, access to necessary information, and the appropriate authorisations.</p></details><details><summary>Can I hire you only to supervise construction?</summary><p>Yes. Construction supervision can be provided as a standalone service with agreed site visits, reporting frequency, responsibilities, and limitations.</p></details><details><summary>Can you help me verify land before purchase?</summary><p>Clapet can coordinate relevant document reviews, official searches, site inspections, and specialist engagements according to the agreed scope. No verification process should be represented as guaranteeing a risk-free transaction.</p></details><details><summary>Do you undertake construction contracts?</summary><p>The company can consider construction assignments within its verified capacity, professional requirements, and contractual scope.</p></details><details><summary>Can you manage agricultural land on my behalf?</summary><p>Yes. Farm management services can be structured around the land, activities, budget, reporting needs, and objectives of the client.</p></details><details><summary>Do you supply goods to institutions and NGOs?</summary><p>Clapet can respond to suitable supply requirements and procurement opportunities within its capacity and the applicable eligibility conditions.</p></details><details><summary>How do I request a quotation?</summary><p>Submit a project brief describing the service required, location, scope, timeline, and available budget information. The team can assess the enquiry and advise on next steps.</p></details><details><summary>Can I monitor my project online?</summary><p>Where the client portal service is available and included in the engagement, authorised clients can view reports, project milestones, documents, and service requests.</p></details><details><summary>How are maintenance costs approved?</summary><p>The owner and Clapet should agree on approval limits and procedures before work begins. The portal can record quotations, approvals, invoices, and completion evidence.</p></details><details><summary>How can I become a supplier or contractor?</summary><p>Submit the partner registration form with relevant company details, service categories, experience, and supporting documents. Registration is subject to review.</p></details></div></div></section>
